# The mistake every other language's sort makes easy: a comparator over two
# elements. Vine's sort takes a key function and calls it with one element at
# a time, so a two-parameter function is an arity error -- which names the
# function and the place it was written, and is the same error map and filter
# give. See Lists in docs/spec.md.
let orders = [{qty: 2}, {qty: 1}]
print(sort(orders, fn(a, b) { a.qty < b.qty }))
